# Atomic-write artifacts from data/csv_safe_write.py (see issue #145)
data/*.csv.bak
data/*.csv.bak*
data/*.csv.tmp

# Project Specific
# known_entities.json (publication + platform name -> host-alias map) is
# committed as reference data so the submission pipeline can resolve
# publications in CI and local runs. Every loader now resolves it to the single
# curated backend/known_entities.json (submission_runtime.config,
# process_submission, rosen_scraper.workflow via find_project_root, and the
# diagnostic/backfill scripts anchored via Path(__file__) — #354).
# schema_builder.py rebuilds the schema to a staging file by default and only
# overwrites the curated file under --write-canonical (keeping a .bak); the
# staging file and that backup are generated artifacts, not tracked.
backend/known_entities.discovered.json
backend/known_entities.json.bak

